{"address":"1226 State St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":null,"classy":null,"divey":true,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":null,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":true,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":true,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":null,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Dive Bars, Sports Bars, Lounges","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"13:0-2:0","Monday":"0:0-0:0","Saturday":"13:0-2:0","Sunday":"13:0-2:0","Thursday":"13:0-2:0","Tuesday":"13:0-2:0","Wednesday":"13:0-2:0"},"name":"The Sportsman","review_info":[{"review_date":"2021-12-28 02:54:43","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"This bar is awesome!  Didn't think much of it at first but our bartender Alice made our experience impeccable. Not only is she a great mixologist, she is down to earth and stole our hearts with her charm.  Thank you for making my birthday one of the most memorable ones.  Best bartender ever!"},{"review_date":"2021-12-09 00:03:34","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"My husband Matt B. and I visited the Sportsman a couple weeks ago for a round of beers after dinner on State Street. We'd been to the Riviera the night before, which took over the Sportsman's old location, and were curious about this place, as it was apparently a Santa Barbara spot that had been around for ages. We stopped by around 10:30 on a Sunday night and it was pretty calm, with an unassuming dive bar atmosphere. There weren't a lot of people and we talked to the bartender for a while, a woman who's been with the bar for quite a long time.

We got a couple of draft beers--two IPAs on tap, I think Figueroa Mountain and Firestone--and played a couple rounds of pool. It's a good thing there weren't a lot of people around because we (and me especially) are absolutely dog shit terrible at pool. I was embarrassed that my own husband was there to witness my astounding lack of coordination. Like if someone wanted to blackmail me with the footage, I would probably be willing to pay. We should never do that in public.

Even so, it was fun, and the beer was good and refreshing. We enjoyed our visit to the Sportsman and would be happy to go back for more beer and maybe pool, as long as no one else is watching."},{"review_date":"2021-11-27 18:51:52","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"We love dive bars, especially when the bartender makes bloody Mary's from scratch! No premix crap! It was a Monday morning and the bloody mary really hit the spot. Very small place but clean. Locals spot, friendly people"}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"508 E Haley St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Jazz & Blues, Music Venues, Arts & Entertainment, Nightlife, Restaurants, Bars, Local Flavor, Bagels, Food, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Dive Bars, Delis, Coffee & Tea","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"6:0-18:0","Monday":"6:0-18:0","Saturday":"8:0-18:0","Thursday":"6:0-18:0","Tuesday":"6:0-18:0","Wednesday":"6:0-18:0"},"name":"Muddy Waters Cafe","review_info":[{"review_date":"2015-09-18 02:36:39","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"So sad to hear Muddy's is closing . Great coffee house, eclectic art and people! Not sure where my go to place will be now......"},{"review_date":"2015-08-09 20:19:08","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"So many little spaces, rooms, and nooks to sit on a chair, couch or table.  Perfect for working, meeting up with friends, hanging out.  Great inside and outside space.  Art focused, which I LOVE!

If I lived closer, this would be a regular spot."},{"review_date":"2015-05-29 06:16:17","review_stars":3.0,"review_text":"Decent coffee at an okay price. Some people like the decorations but I thought it was kind of messy and had a grandma-esque vibe too it. 

I got my usual, an iced coffee and HOT DAMN. It was strong...like a too strong for my tastes. I will come back to try their other drinks though. Not giving up on this place just yet!"}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"3967 State St Space 4, Space 4","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":3.5,"categories":"Sandwiches, Breakfast & Brunch, Restaurants, Fast Food","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"8:0-22:0","Monday":"8:0-22:0","Saturday":"8:0-22:0","Sunday":"9:0-21:0","Thursday":"8:0-22:0","Tuesday":"8:0-22:0","Wednesday":"8:0-22:0"},"name":"Subway","review_info":[{"review_date":"2020-11-02 05:34:38","review_stars":3.0,"review_text":"My kid loves Subway. I appreciate their wide selection, their consistency, and their price point, which is dirt cheap for SB. Chances are you like it too, or it wouldn't be the largest fast-food franchise in the country by number of stores. I wish there were 3.5 stars, because that seems more fair. 

This shop is tiny and tucked away in the 5 points center. They have a few tables out front, but it's not a great place to eat unless you're really hungry. They are generally very friendly, although one time I forgot to ask for my free cookie up front and they refused to give it to me. Their cookies aren't any good anyways so they can keep it, but it seemed like a silly decision. Maybe I'll get my kid to TP the place when she's a teenager. 

Anyway, Valentinos, South Coast, Sam's, Plaza Deli, and Fresco all have better sandwiches but not as cheap and maybe your kids love Subway too. Certainly a reasonable option."},{"review_date":"2020-04-21 23:17:40","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Sandwiches were really good wasn't expecting much but honestly as blown away keep up the good work"},{"review_date":"2016-03-31 19:45:20","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"The employees didn't seem to care, they also didn't cut the bread correctly and the sandwich was falling apart. Make the trip to another subway, it'll be worth it."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"Canary Hotel, 31 W Carrillo St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":true,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":true,"valet":true,"validated":true},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":false,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":3.5,"categories":"Restaurants, Event Planning & Services, American (New), Party & Event Planning, American (Traditional)","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"7:0-23:0","Monday":"7:0-22:0","Saturday":"7:0-23:0","Sunday":"7:0-22:0","Thursday":"7:0-22:0","Tuesday":"7:0-22:0","Wednesday":"7:0-22:0"},"name":"Coast Restaurant & Bar","review_info":[{"review_date":"2015-06-28 02:55:51","review_stars":3.0,"review_text":"My wife and I went for a special evening out.  The lounge setting and ambience was wonderful and relaxing. The dinning room had subtle elegance.  The bread was warm and tasty, butternut squash soup and the romaine wedge salad was delicious. The service was outstanding. All was wonderful until the main course. The short  ribs tasted like pot roast and the New York steak was ok-needed salt.  We really wanted it to be great but the main dishes lacked flavor. Now for dessert... Butterscotch pudding and lemon cheesecake were excellent.  We really wanted to give 4 stars but 3 is all we can give it."},{"review_date":"2013-03-20 03:27:00","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"We were all very tired after a long day of work and being on the road, so we decided to try the restaurant in our hotel, which was conveniently located in our hotel's lobby.

We started our evening sharing the roasted California mussels seasoned perfectly and served with sourdough bread.  Then for our main course my daughter and I shared the savory manilla clams served over hand cut tagliatelle seasoned with basil, lemon and chile.  My husband ordered the crisy duck breast over potato gnocci and told both the waiter and I how he was in heaven that they had created a dish with two of his favorite meals put together in one.  We topped off the night with a bottle of Conundrum wine and a serving of their warm, comforting bread pudding and ice cream and called it a night!

The service was friendly and quick, and the food was delicious.  We will definitely be back the next time we're visiting the wonderful city of Santa Barbara!"},{"review_date":"2013-03-16 18:15:54","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"We decided to eat at Coast tonight because we wanted to try something different in Santa Barbara.  We ordered  the mussels, the pork belly sliders, shishito peppers and the pork ribs everything we had was really very good but the real stand out were the mussels the sauce was accompanied with a sourdough toast that was delicious.  Just before we left James Siao the head chef came out and talked to us we told him how he really enjoyed the meal."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"211 Helena Ave","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":true,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":false,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Food, Bars, Tapas Bars, Restaurants, Pubs, Wine Bars, Nightlife, Coffee & Tea","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"15:0-1:0","Saturday":"13:0-1:0","Sunday":"13:0-1:0","Thursday":"15:0-1:0","Tuesday":"15:0-1:0","Wednesday":"15:0-1:0"},"name":"Reds Bin 211","review_info":[{"review_date":"2016-04-30 05:17:13","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Reds Bin is a chill lil spot in Santa Barbara I have come to frequent. If you get sick of the State Street scene and want a bit of a different, more relaxed vibe, I would go to Reds. The bar food is also super yummy, and the bartenders are lovely people. I really love this place."},{"review_date":"2016-04-23 01:42:23","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"Not a fan of a place who likes to serve alcohol to underage kids...... Prob should think bout hiring some new bartenders."},{"review_date":"2016-03-29 22:03:46","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"This place was so fun. Great cocktails. Great vibe. 

My boyfriend and I hung out here while we were visiting Santa Barbara on a saturday night. There was ample seating (which is a huge deal to me). 

The bartenders were super great and it seemed like a place for locals. Not touristy which was great."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"1482 E Valley Rd","attributes":{"Ambience":null,"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":null,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":null,"RestaurantsReservations":null,"RestaurantsTakeOut":false,"WiFi":null},"business_stars":3.0,"categories":"Specialty Food, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Grocery, Bakeries, Restaurants, Delis, Butcher, Food","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"7:0-20:0","Monday":"7:0-20:0","Saturday":"7:0-20:0","Sunday":"7:0-20:0","Thursday":"7:0-20:0","Tuesday":"7:0-20:0","Wednesday":"7:0-20:0"},"name":"Montecito Village Grocery","review_info":[{"review_date":"2021-12-15 18:18:53","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"Montecito Village Grocery  was apparently my husband's mother's go-to grocery store. Smaller with less inventory than the big chain groceries in town, but also an easier place to shop, as it never gets crowded. I've been to the Von's on Coast Village Road many times over the years--it's pretty convenient, after all, and impossible to miss if you spend any time in Montecito. By contrast, I'd never even seen this market until Matt B. suggested we go to pick up a few odd things we needed for the week.

It's a cute place with some comfortable neighborhood charm, and I enjoyed the ample parking and calm, quiet atmosphere. Obviously, the stock was more limited than at a supermarket--we couldn't find the pasta we wanted and did end up making a Von's run later in the week--but we picked up some of the items on our list, including a few bottles of wine. The wine selection was solid, with lots of local/regional wines. Definitely extensive enough that you'll walk away with what you need if you're not looking for anything too specific. (Our toddler, who was just learning his colors, pointed to a wall of reds and said, "Red? Red?") The cheese/deli section was pretty enticing, too.

Check-out was quick and easy and we went home with enough provisions to see us through dinner that night (mostly, we needed wine). I like Vons fine, but it's nice to have Montecito Village Grocery as a pleasant, less busy alternative."},{"review_date":"2021-08-08 12:02:22","review_stars":2.0,"review_text":"Bad service and expired products, its always hit or miss there, your better off going to Von's."},{"review_date":"2019-09-10 15:53:32","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"This neighborhood grocery store has awesome European speciality items, not found elsewhere.  From the Deli to yogurt, olives, to plant-based products: it provides quality food at its finest.  We've become accustomed to settle for the adjacent and lower quality in our diets: not cool.  Treat yourself, this grocery store is Delectable."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"111 State St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":null,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":false,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"no"},"business_stars":3.0,"categories":"Restaurants, Pizza","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"11:0-0:0","Monday":"0:0-0:0","Saturday":"11:0-0:0","Sunday":"11:0-0:0","Thursday":"11:0-0:0","Tuesday":"11:0-20:0","Wednesday":"11:0-0:0"},"name":"Rusty's Pizza Parlor","review_info":[{"review_date":"2022-01-18 19:14:33","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Really good pizza, reasonable prices, nice setting, late hours, quick pickup....."},{"review_date":"2022-01-06 21:11:26","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"Garbage customer service. Owner should just have a self order computer at the counter.Pizza was decent. Don't come here."},{"review_date":"2021-12-12 01:30:37","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"Had a homeless person in here eating, shopping cart and all. Kids are riding around indoors on electric scooters. Staff are unfriendly and unresponsive. Service is slow. 

They must be really underpaid or something because it really seems like no one cares at all here. 

Best part of my visit today was find a finger nail in my salad. I'm a dude, it's a a chick's finger nail. Did they seriously not wear gloves when servicing the salad bar or something? People are probably chewing their finger nails while making my food. Disgusting."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"30 E Victoria St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":null,"classy":null,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":null,"romantic":null,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":null,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":null,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"no"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Italian, Restaurants","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"17:0-22:0","Saturday":"17:0-22:0","Sunday":"17:0-21:0","Thursday":"17:0-21:0","Tuesday":"17:0-21:0","Wednesday":"17:0-21:0"},"name":"Trattoria Vittoria","review_info":[{"review_date":"2022-01-09 04:55:39","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Great italian food. came here on a whim and thorough enjoyed it. will return next time i'm visiting santa barbara."},{"review_date":"2021-12-11 08:50:25","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Their homemade pasta dishes, lasagna, tortellini and ravioli with a heavenly tomato sauce was definitely one of the most delicious dishes I've tried (and then I've been to Italy). The servers where so funny and genuine, too. We'll be back in SB when we get the chance!"},{"review_date":"2021-12-08 17:23:35","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"We had an early dinner here. It filled up fast so if you can make reservations you should. 

We had an awesome dinner. Atmosphere was perfect.  Wine was delicious and the service was great. 

Next time I will come early and have a drink at the bar. Looked like a fun crowd. Enjoy!"}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"409 State St","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":false,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":null,"Music":true,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":null,"RestaurantsTakeOut":null,"WiFi":null},"business_stars":3.5,"categories":"Nightlife, Bars, American (New), Restaurants, Cocktail Bars","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"16:0-1:0","Saturday":"10:0-1:0","Sunday":"10:0-1:0","Thursday":"16:0-1:0","Tuesday":"16:0-1:0","Wednesday":"16:0-1:0"},"name":"Blind Tiger","review_info":[{"review_date":"2016-04-10 03:56:06","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"Saw the DTease last night and was blown away !! The club is not your usual dive it's has a great design and feel!! The show was amazing with great sound talented artist with great originals can't understand why the place was not sold out !!"},{"review_date":"2015-11-01 04:54:45","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"First time in Blind Tiger to check out the open mic on Wednesday. Very clean, no rank smell - this is important - and tasteful comfortable furnishings. The stage is very pro w good sound system and lighting. When I went to the bar the server was very friendly and relaxed - I liked that too. Our non-alcoholic drinks were tasty and imaginative and he offered us free refills! Not all the acts were great, but a couple really were good and the in house MC was also a strong performer. We'll be back for sure."},{"review_date":"2015-09-01 16:09:43","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"I just moved here and this is my first yelp review. I decided to make one and start with a review of Blind Tiger. I've been to 3 different bars since I got into town and Blind Tiger was definitely my favorite. 

I came on with one of my girlfriends on Saturday. There was a $10 cover but the accommodating staff and great crowd made it all worth it. Brandon was so informative and fun and made our entire experience memorable. 

We will definitely be back to dance and party with everyone!!!!"}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"1201 State St","attributes":{"Ambience":null,"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":false,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":null},"business_stars":3.0,"categories":"Bars, Restaurants, Nightlife, Barbeque","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":null,"name":"State & A Bar and Grill","review_info":[{"review_date":"2012-07-17 01:38:31","review_stars":2.0,"review_text":"Flashback!  My old happy hour spot. Great outdoor patio. Glad I got one last visit in. They are closed now and new restaurant is on the way."},{"review_date":"2012-06-14 14:12:39","review_stars":2.0,"review_text":"food was good, maybe a little over priced, but what they lacked in quality they made up for in customer service."},{"review_date":"2011-04-13 11:15:00","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"I seriously thought I was on candid camera or something.  I came in for a late lunch one day and everything I got here was absolutely wretched...even their drinks!

Its such a shame because they have a great location and a nice outdoor patio...how do they stay in business??

I must say this place also gets an award: the absolute worst calamari I've ever sampled in my life (and that's saying something)."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"5711 Calle Real","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":true,"street":false,"valet":false,"validated":false},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":true,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":3.0,"categories":"American (New), Italian, Restaurants, Pizza","city":"Goleta","hours":{"Friday":"16:30-21:30","Monday":"16:30-21:0","Saturday":"16:30-21:0","Sunday":"16:30-21:0","Thursday":"16:30-21:0","Tuesday":"16:30-21:0","Wednesday":"16:30-21:0"},"name":"Petrini's Restaurant","review_info":[{"review_date":"2016-09-02 07:51:10","review_stars":5.0,"review_text":"I tend not to expect much from food locations in Strip Malls.  While staying in the Santa Barbara area, I just wanted a good piece of Pizza. We stopped here while on a walk and ordered an onion and cheese pizza, small size.  Neither of us could believe how fresh and great it was! The sauce was a good homemade red with Italian spices and fresh tomato flavor. Just enough good cheese.  We stopped in twice after having such great luck.  Tried the salads, pasta and more pizza, garlic bread and wine.  Family owned and run place that's cordial and homey.   This is the kind of place you find in Chicago and New York. Just a little gem with friendly people and really good Italian food!"},{"review_date":"2016-08-17 01:35:09","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"Well, I tried eating at this Petrini's again, and I'm really sad to report that the food has gotten worse AND more expensive. The Chicken Picatta was drowning in butter, or grease; I'm not sure what that was. The fettuccine Alfredo that came with it was undercooked and had zero taste. We also were served garlic bread that was burned to black. To make things worse, I took the food home because I just could eat it at the restaurant. I was hungry later so I ate it. 
Oh My God.....I couldn't keep it down. I got such a stomach ache from that food. Petrini's , you are a local restaurant and I really try to support local businesses, but you are bad for my health."},{"review_date":"2016-07-11 15:51:04","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"I have not been in here for many years, but we stopped in the other night and it was tasty traditional american italian food for a great price. The meat raviolis were very tender and delicious and the sauce was spot on. The spaghetti and meatballs (the yard stick for any italian review) were also very good. I also really enjoyed my cup of minestrone soup, really hit the spot. The waiters were very attentive and the place had a very welcoming and tidy atmosphere. 

The only downside, the water tasted horrible, I think they need to replace their filter or something."}],"state":"CA"}

{"address":"217 G Stearns Wharf","attributes":{"Ambience":{"casual":true,"classy":false,"divey":false,"hipster":false,"intimate":false,"romantic":false,"touristy":false,"trendy":false,"upscale":false},"BusinessParking":{"garage":false,"lot":false,"street":true,"valet":true,"validated":true},"Music":null,"OutdoorSeating":true,"RestaurantsGoodForGroups":true,"RestaurantsReservations":null,"RestaurantsTakeOut":true,"WiFi":"free"},"business_stars":4.0,"categories":"Bars, Venues & Event Spaces, Event Planning & Services, Wine Tasting Room, Arts & Entertainment, Food, Wine Bars, Beer, Wine & Spirits, Nightlife, Wineries","city":"Santa Barbara","hours":{"Friday":"11:0-21:0","Monday":"11:0-20:0","Saturday":"11:0-21:0","Sunday":"11:0-20:0","Thursday":"11:0-20:0","Tuesday":"11:0-20:0","Wednesday":"11:0-20:0"},"name":"Deep Sea Tasting Room","review_info":[{"review_date":"2021-12-18 00:53:58","review_stars":4.0,"review_text":"Beautiful beautiful view and friendly staff. We went on a rainy morning and still enjoyed the view. Wines are serviceable but it's really about the view."},{"review_date":"2021-12-03 20:29:36","review_stars":3.0,"review_text":"It's a great location to have a drink. Beautiful views. Good breeze. It's unfortunate that the wine isn't as good as the location."},{"review_date":"2021-12-01 23:32:42","review_stars":1.0,"review_text":"Good Afternoon,

I am again submitting this review in reference to prior feedback i offered regarding an unfortunate very racially charged incident at Deep Sea Tasting room. To date the venue has still made no attempt at reaching out to me to discuss this rather u fortunate encounter with management that resulted in me cancelling my membership and not returning.

I wish the follow-up on the part of the leadership was as good as the view from the tasting room."}],"state":"CA"}
